						},
						{
							"_type": "UMLUseCase",
							"_id": "AAAAAAABH57k",
							"_parent": {
								"$ref": "AAAAAAAByxlx"
							},
							"name": "Register for Course",
							"ownedElements": [
								{
									"_type": "UMLInclude",
									"_id": "AAAAAAABI506",
									"_parent": {
										"$ref": "AAAAAAABH57k"
									},
									"source": {
										"$ref": "AAAAAAABH57k"
									},
									"target": {
										"$ref": "AAAAAAABwnZN"
									}
								},
								{
									"_type": "UMLInclude",
									"_id": "AAAAAAAB0ScV",
									"_parent": {
										"$ref": "AAAAAAABH57k"
									},
									"source": {
										"$ref": "AAAAAAABH57k"
									},
									"target": {
										"$ref": "AAAAAAABYL4x"
									}
								}
							],
							"documentation": "FULLY DRESSED USE CASE: Register for Course\nScope: Smart Academic and Examination Management System (SAEMS)\nLevel: User goal\nPrimary actor: Student\nSecondary actors: Identity Authentication Service, Bank Payment Gateway, Email/SMS Notification Service\nStakeholders and interests: Student - register quickly and correctly; Department Coordinator - only eligible students enrolled / exceptions reviewed; University - dues collected, seat limits respected.\nPreconditions: 1) Student is logged in (identity verified through the Identity Authentication Service). 2) Course is offered in the current registration period.\nSuccess guarantee (postconditions): Student is enrolled in the course and a seat is allocated; a registration confirmation is generated; the student's timetable is updated; a success notification is sent.\nMinimal guarantee: No partial enrolment is stored; if registration is not completed the student's record and seat count are unchanged.\nTrigger: Student selects a course and chooses Register.\n\nMAIN SUCCESS SCENARIO\n1. Student selects a course from search results/course details and requests registration.\n2. System verifies the student's identity (active session) and performs <<include>> Check Registration Eligibility (prerequisites satisfied, seat available, no outstanding dues).\n3. System confirms the student is eligible.\n4. System enrols the student and reduces the available seat count.\n5. System generates a registration confirmation and updates the student's timetable.\n6. System performs <<include>> Send Notification (email/SMS) to the student.\n7. System displays the registration confirmation. Use case ends.\n\nEXTENSIONS (ALTERNATIVE FLOWS)\n2a. Prerequisites not satisfied: (<<extend>> Request Special Registration)\n    2a1. System informs the student which prerequisites are missing and offers a special registration request.\n    2a2. Student submits the request; it is forwarded to the Department Coordinator (Review Special Registration). Registration is pending.\n    2a3. Coordinator approves -> resume at step 4; Coordinator rejects -> system sends a rejection notification and the use case ends in failure.\n2b. Course is full: (<<extend>> Join Waiting List)\n    2b1. System informs the student that no seats are available and offers a waiting list.\n    2b2. Student accepts; system adds the student to the waiting list. Use case ends.\n2c. Student has outstanding dues: (<<extend>> Pay Outstanding Dues)\n    2c1. System asks the student to clear the dues before completing registration.\n    2c2. Student pays through the Bank Payment Gateway, which returns the payment result to SAEMS.\n    2c2a. Payment fails/cancelled: system informs the student; registration is not completed. Use case ends.\n    2c3. Payment successful: resume at step 4.\n2d. Identity cannot be verified / session expired: system redirects the student to Log In; use case restarts after successful authentication.\n4a. Last seat taken by another student while this request is processed: system re-evaluates and continues at 2b.\n6a. Notification service unavailable: system logs the failure and retries later; registration remains valid.\n\nSpecial requirements: Eligibility check and enrolment must be atomic (no overbooking); payment result must be received before enrolment; confirmation shown within 3 seconds under normal load.\nFrequency of use: Very high during registration periods.\nOpen issues: Waiting-list promotion rules (automatic vs manual) to be decided."
						},
