							},
							"name": "View Timetable"
						},
						{
							"_type": "UMLUseCase",
							"_id": "AAAAAAABC+y1",
							"_parent": {
								"$ref": "AAAAAAAByxlx"
							},
							"name": "Drop Course"
						}
					],
					"documentation": "System boundary = SAEMS. Actors are outside the boundary.\nPrimary actors: Student, Course Instructor, Department Coordinator, Examination Officer, System Administrator (all human; generalized by the abstract actor 'University User', who owns Log In; one person may play several roles).\nSecondary actors (external systems): Identity Authentication Service, Bank Payment Gateway, Email/SMS Notification Service.\n\nDeliberately NOT modeled as use cases / relationships:\n- Verify identity (covered by Log In), Verify prerequisites, Check seat availability, Check dues -> internal checks grouped into the included use case 'Check Registration Eligibility'.\n- Generate registration confirmation, Update timetable, Reduce seat count, Display error message, Store results of payment -> internal system activities, described inside the Register for Course flow.\n- Approve / Reject as separate use cases -> outcomes of 'Review Special Registration' / 'Review Special Drop Request'.\n- Students/Instructors are not associated with Send Notification (they are recipients, not actors that trigger it).\n- Log In is not <<include>>d by every use case (precondition instead) to avoid clutter.\n- Pay Outstanding Dues is not included, it is an <<extend>> (only when dues exist). Same for Join Waiting List, Special requests, Recover Password, Correct Incomplete Marks, Modify Examination Schedule.\n- No association between secondary actors and use cases they do not take part in."
				},
				{
					"_type": "UMLActor",
					"_id": "AAAAAAABCgc0",
					"_parent": {
						"$ref": "AAAAAAABEyze"
					},
					"name": "University User",
					"ownedElements": [
						{
							"_type": "UMLAssociation",
							"_id": "AAAAAAABGDHR",
							"_parent": {
